 "notes": "<h3>Living &amp; dining</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><b>Sofa</b> against the kitchen wall, chaise toward the dining area. <b>TV stand</b> on the office wall facing it, about 91 cm of walkway between the two zones.</li>\n        <li><b>Coffee table</b> in front of the seat, next to the chaise. Only about 14 cm from the seat: sliding it 15 to 20 cm toward the TV gives more knee room and still leaves about 70 cm to walk.</li>\n        <li><b>Bookshelf (dining)</b> beside the TV stand, <b>Bookshelf 2</b> by the kitchen door.</li>\n        <li><b>Dining table</b> against the kitchen-side wall, so chairs pull out on three sides. <b>Piano</b> on the opposite wall, with <b>Bookshelf 1</b> next to it near the entrance. <b>Shoe rack</b> just inside the entrance.</li>\n        <li><b>Kitchen shelf unit</b> below the kitchen door, about 68 cm from the L-shaped counter.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Master bedroom</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><b>Wardrobe (to buy)</b> in the recess: up to 140 × 60 cm. Measure the height under the bulkhead before buying.</li>\n        <li><b>Bed</b> headboard on the outer wall, with the <b>bedstand</b> beside it and about 63 cm at the foot to reach the utility platform door. The window wall stays clear.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Daughter's room</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><b>Wardrobe</b> beside the door, <b>bed</b> along the master bedroom wall, <b>bedside table</b> by the window.</li>\n        <li>The window sill is low and one pane opens: fit a window restrictor, and keep climbable furniture away from the window where possible.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Office</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><b>Desk</b> under the window with 75 cm of chair space, <b>Bookshelf 3</b> on the wall shared with your daughter's room.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <h3>Helper's room</h3>\n      <ul><li><b>Helper bed</b> (175 × 80 cm) along the long wall, head at the far end. Its foot reaches into the door swing, so it shows red: the door opens to about 50°, leaving roughly 65 cm to pass. A door rehung to open outward, or a folding door, would clear it fully.</li>\n        <li>Keep the wall cabinet by the door reachable: nothing tall in front of it.</li></ul>"
